      "writtenOn": "2023-08-14T13:05:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This uploaded patch only contains a subset of functionality of the proposed Secretkeeper. \n\nWeaver, IIUC, is essentially a key-value storage, used by services like LockSettingsService to (securely) maintain a map (where the \u0027value\u0027 is confidential). These keys \u0026 values are known to system_server \u0026 the weaver is used for providing persistence.\n\n1. (b/291228560) Secretkeeper should be robust against MITM attacks. We use Sk for storing the secrets of pVM. These should not be known to the host even when they are being `stored`. To ensure this, we will establish a secure channel (on the top of untrusted channel, i.e. host) between 2 end points (pVM \u0026 TA backing the Secretkeeper HAL). This ISecureConnectionEstablishment will also be part of Secretkeeper. Therefore, the store/read function parameters will be serialized COSE objects that contain encrypted secrets (we encrypt secrets using the shared master secrets) and additional data (like Dice chain, Dice policy) used to authenticate the client.\nAuthentication scheme will also be part of Secretkeeper spec.\n\n2. (b/294177871) Secretkeeper will also expose Garbage collection API to allow host to delete entries if VMs are deleted and/or the apps owning the pVM is uninstalled. (This required to ensure Secretkeeper\u0027s storage does not grow without bounds).\n\n\nApologies for the TODO bug, that should\u0027ve been b/291224769",
      "parentUuid": "070c8318_acfe2cae",
      "revId": "bb025cd4dfaa7fb40a2c14cf722ca878d08d6b5d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
